WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.650
London and Mumbai sit
on different continents,

2
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.570
in very different countries.

3
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.770
Researchers at Loughborough University
rank cities around the world.

4
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.070
London and Mumbai both
rank high on their list.

5
00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:19.610
In 2021, 40.6 per cent of London's
residents were born outside the UK.

6
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.710
So what ties each city so
tightly to the rest of the world?

7
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.130
Is it their airports?

8
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.130
Their banks?

9
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.180
Their films?

10
00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:30.910
In this mission, you'll see
how globalisation links places,

11
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:36.070
through flows of goods, money,
people, ideas and media.

12
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.790
Then you'll see how each city
connects, place by place,

13
00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.530
on maps of London and Mumbai.

14
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:47.590
Your mission: find out what ties London
and Mumbai so tightly to the rest of the

15
00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.270
world.
